  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Selvaraj vs The District Collector on 31 August, 2017 Bench: K.K.Sasidharan, G.R.Swaminathan Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 31.08.2017 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice K.K.Sasidharan and The Honourable Mr.Justice G.R.Swaminathan W.P.(MD)No.2390 of 2013 M.Selvaraj .. Petitioner Vs. 1.The District Collector, Madurai. 2.The District Supply Officer, Madurai. 3.The Taluk Supply Officer, Madurai.",
    "facts": "The petitioner filed this Writ Petition to direct the respondents not to interfere in his business of sale of non-edible oil products under the name and style of Vetrivel Gingelly oil and Thanga Mayil Groundnut oil except under due process of law. 2.It is the grievance of the petitioner that the respondents had initiated action by seizing of the products without following due process of law. The petitioner, therefore, filed this writ petition for issuance of a Writ of Mandamus directing the respondents not to seal the premises pursuant to the action taken to seize the product on allegation that he is indulged in sale of non-edible oil under the guise of edible oils.",
